claims:
1. A system comprising one or more computers and one or more storage devices, the one or more storage devices storing instructions that, when executed by the one or more computers, cause the one or more computers to perform operations comprising:
accessing a record of click data that includes data for clicks submitted by multiple different users on search results provided by a search system;
determining, from the record of click data for clicks submitted by multiple different users, for each of a plurality of address-based groups of resources, a respective count of repeat clicks for the address-based group of resources,
wherein each group is defined by an Internet address and the respective resources in the group are accessible using the Internet address,
wherein each repeat click is a click made by a respective user on any one of the resources in the group after a previous click on the same resource by the same respective user, and
wherein only one click from any given user is counted as a repeat click on each group of resources,
whereby if the same user has submitted multiple clicks that would be considered repeat clicks for any group of resources, only one of those clicks is used in the count of repeat clicks on the group of resources;

determining, for each of the plurality of address-based groups of resources, a respective group-based modification factor for the address-based group of resources using the count of repeat clicks for the address-based group of resources;
receiving a search query from a client device;
receiving search result data identifying a first plurality of search result resources returned in response to the search query and respective initial scores for each of the first plurality of search result resources;
identifying a respective address-based group of resources to which each of the search result resources belongs; and
adjusting the initial score for each of the search result resources based at least in part on the group-specific modification factor for the address-based group of resources to which the search result resource belongs to generate a respective second score for each of the search result resources.

7. The system of claim 1, the operations further comprising:
identifying a first click by a particular user on a first search result during a first search session, wherein the first search result is provided to the particular user in response to a first search query, and wherein the first search result identifies a particular resource in the group of resources;
identifying a second click by the particular user on a second search result during a different, second search session, wherein the second search result is provided to the particular user in response to a second search query, wherein text of the first search query matches text of the second search query, and wherein the second search result identifies the particular resource;
determining that the time between the first click and the second click exceeds a predetermined threshold time;
counting the second click by the particular user as a repeat click on the group of resources;
identifying a third click by the particular user on a third search result during a different, third search session, wherein the third search result is provided to the particular user in response to a third search query, wherein text of the first search query matches text of the third search query, and wherein the third search result identifies the particular resource;
determining that the second click by the particular user has been counted as a repeat click on the group of resources; and
refraining from counting the third click by the particular user as a repeat click on the group of resources.

